+  //A diagnostic, not a setting. With bootProbe on, the machine prints
+  //everything the cartridge's own boot code can see at the instant it is handed
+  //control, once, and says no more. run-gate.sh runs the machine twice - booted
+  //from a real PIF ROM, and from PIF::bootHLE - and compares the two, which is
+  //the only way to check an HLE boot against the thing it stands in for.
+  //Nothing in a shipped core turns it on.
+  bool bootProbe = false;
+  bool bootProbeDone = false;
